of a rooted tree or arborescence: each vertex’s heavy child is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its child with the largest subtree (the first in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order on a tie), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heavy edges form paths. Vertices get positions in a preorder that takes the heavy child first,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so each heavy path and each subtree is an interval of positions, and any path between two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices is at most 2⌊log₂ n⌋ + 1 intervals ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"segments(from:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), for path and subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries over a structure indexed by position."}]},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/HeavyLightDecomposition/Segment/init(positions:isReversed:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition\/segment\/init(positions:isreversed:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition\/Segment\/init(positions:isReversed:)","type":"topic","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"positions","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Range","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sn"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isReversed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","title":"init(positions:isReversed:)"}}}